+- **Defect:** Cypress acceptance test failures due to `render()` rebuilding all `<li>` via `innerHTML = ''` on every toggle interaction, detaching DOM nodes that the browser test held references to.
+- **Scantling:** `assets/toggle-identity-scantling.json` — defines the DOM-element-identity contract for the toggle-to-do seam.
+- **Contract scenario:** `features/dom-identity.feature:3` — `@contract` scenario that must pass before the perturbation is resolved.
+- **Perturbations planted:** 3 `// PERTURBATION` markers in `js/app.js` at the toggle single item, toggle-all, and clear-completed handler seams.
+- **Watchbill:** Created `watchbill.json` with the dom-identity contract watch.
+- **Fix approach (for QM/Crew):** Mutate existing `<li>` nodes in-place instead of calling `render()` which does `innerHTML = ''`. Toggle `li.classList` and the child `.toggle` checkbox property on the existing element. Retain `render()` only for structural changes (new-todo, destroy, clear-completed where elements are removed).
+- **Next role:** QM — verify the contract scenario passes against the current code (it likely won't since the fix isn't applied yet — it's a design-phase contract that will be proven when Crew implements), then dispatch Crew to implement the fix, then QM again to confirm all scenarios pass.
+- **Working tree:** Clean, no pending commits.
